        "original_id": "281e258f-b174-52ee-b39d-bcad6a0fa2e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Ugni, Stenomesson\n- Families: Myrtaceae, Amaryllidaceae\n- Places: western Latin America, southern Chile, Juan Fernández Islands, southern Argentina, southern Mexico, western South America, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, northern Chile\n\nFacts:\n- Ugni is a genus of plants in the myrtle family Myrtaceae, and it was described as a genus in 1848.\n- Ugni is native to western Latin America, ranging from the Valdivian temperate rain forests of southern Chile, including the Juan Fernández Islands, and adjacent regions of southern Argentina north to southern Mexico.\n- Stenomesson is a genus of bulbous plants in the family Amaryllidaceae.\n- All species of Stenomesson are native to western South America, including Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, and northern Chile.",
